<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>Latest news from the Middle East, daily international news reports - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage and analyses of political and social issues across the Middle East, including Egypt, the Gulf states, Iraq, Israel, Jordan, Lebanon, Saudi Arabia, Syria, Yemen and beyond.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/</link><lastBuildDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 20:59:40 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category></category><title>Black smoke seen near Riyadh amid air raid alerts in Saudi Arabia</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/black-smoke-seen-near-riyadh-amid-air-raid-alerts-in-saudi-arabia</link><description>
⁠Flames and plumes of smoke ‌were ⁠seen ‌rising near ⁠Riyadh airport this afternoon with flights cancelled and delayed. This as fighting between Saudi-backed government forces and Iran-backed Houthi rebels has killed 48 people in recent hours. The rebels staged a lightning offensive this month, seizing swathes of territory in Yemen and launching a barrage of missiles and drones toward Saudi Arabia. Details and analysis by FRANCE 24 international affairs editor, Jamie Smith-Maillet.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6756645e-b43c-11f1-8e27-9ff5c3f464d4/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260919-160101-160431-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6756645e-b43c-11f1-8e27-9ff5c3f464d4/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260919-160101-160431-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6c85b75e-b43c-11f1-b045-e125042f2034</guid><pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 15:16:03 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Saudi Arabia says air defences intercepted Houthi ballistic missile targeting Riyadh</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260919-smoke-flames-seen-near-riyadh-airport-major-flight-disruptions-reported</link><description>
Saudi Arabia on Saturday confirmed that Yemen’s Houthi rebels tried to attack its capital with a ballistic missile, the first targeting of Riyadh since the escalation in fighting with the rebels. The confirmation came hours after the Houthis said they targeted "sensitive sites" in Saudi Arabia.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/40a51f4e-b423-11f1-bcd8-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-19T114802Z-1980126111-RC28MNAXZ2HR-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-YEMEN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/40a51f4e-b423-11f1-bcd8-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-19T114802Z-1980126111-RC28MNAXZ2HR-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-YEMEN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1ccc705c-b425-11f1-bb34-a7096373d88d</guid><pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 12:53:19 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/40a51f4e-b423-11f1-bcd8-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-19T114802Z-1980126111-RC28MNAXZ2HR-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-YEMEN.jpg">© Reuters via stringer</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israel: 'NAZA' documentary sparks political storm</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260919-israel-naza-documentary-sparks-political-storm</link><description>
The documentary film 'NAZA', and its co-directors Yuval Abraham and Rachel Szor, are at the centre of a controversy in Israel.The film, which won an award at the Venice Film Festival, features anonymous Israeli sources accusing the military of intentionally killing numerous civilians in Gaza.Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said on Wednesday that he intended to "strip of their citizenship" those who "defame" the Israeli army.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/74111114-b426-11f1-9220-9ff5c3f464d4/w:1024/p:16x9/Vignette-RS.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/74111114-b426-11f1-9220-9ff5c3f464d4/w:1024/p:16x9/Vignette-RS.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9989a406-b426-11f1-ab3c-af9045de5f47</guid><pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 12:41:53 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>More than 112,000 displaced in Yemen as Houthis seize more ground</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/more-than-112-000-displaced-in-yemen-as-houthis-seize-more-ground</link><description>
Pro-Houthi demonstrations erupted in Yemen after Saudi Arabia accused the military group of targeting the Muslim holy site of Mecca. Story by Elitsa Gadeva.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a4e9a5ae-b407-11f1-b2e8-9ff5c3f464d4/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-18T131305Z-414222399-RC2OLNAJ0IX0-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-YEMEN-HOUTHIS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a4e9a5ae-b407-11f1-b2e8-9ff5c3f464d4/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-18T131305Z-414222399-RC2OLNAJ0IX0-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-YEMEN-HOUTHIS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3451f910-b405-11f1-9cb8-2d26d5c2c2ec</guid><pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 08:57:59 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The World This Week</category><title><![CDATA[AI: Silicon Species or Trojan Horse? Riyadh Calling, Russia Votes & the Ed Sheeran debate]]></title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20260918-time-to-stop-suggesting-ai-is-conscious-riyadh-calling-saudi-s-hour-of-news-russian-elections</link><description>
This week, Saudi Arabia has turned to its allies for military support as Iran-backed Houthi rebels tighten their grip on Yemen’s Red Sea coast and the Bab el Mandeb shipping choke point, while drone attacks on the Kingdom’s oil infrastructure deepen an emerging energy crisis. In Russia, voters head to the polls for a tightly controlled parliamentary election with little meaningful opposition, as Putin insists there will be no new mobilisation. Meanwhile, warnings about the risks of AI are coming from inside the industry itself, with Microsoft AI chief Mustafa Suleyman warning against treating AI models like humans—and raising the prospect of a new “silicon species” competing with us for resources. Finally, in Britain, the royal family is back on the defensive as Earl Spencer’s new claims about Princess Diana’s funeral prompt an unusually pointed response from Buckingham Palace.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/db7520f4-b393-11f1-a724-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/ANTHROPIC.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/db7520f4-b393-11f1-a724-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/ANTHROPIC.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f2bd469a-b395-11f1-9f75-d9cba0bb1897</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 19:20:00 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Gavin LEE</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>US approves $24.3 billion sale of 48 F-35 warplanes to Saudi Arabia</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260918-us-approves-24-3-billion-sale-of-48-f-35-warplanes-to-saudi-arabia</link><description>
The United States on Thursday said it had approved a $24.3 billion sale of 48 F-35 stealth warplanes to Saudi Arabia. Israel has previously voiced concerns about Riyadh buying F-35s, despite a push to normalise relations.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b5501408-b328-11f1-82fe-1d1125ed9143/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-09T121806Z-145721001-RC2OFNAVWHNC-RTRMADP-3-NORWAY-ROYALS-KING-HARALD-FUNERAL.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b5501408-b328-11f1-82fe-1d1125ed9143/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-09T121806Z-145721001-RC2OFNAVWHNC-RTRMADP-3-NORWAY-ROYALS-KING-HARALD-FUNERAL.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0e13024a-b328-11f1-b171-f5081862f07e</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 06:29:47 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b5501408-b328-11f1-82fe-1d1125ed9143/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-09T121806Z-145721001-RC2OFNAVWHNC-RTRMADP-3-NORWAY-ROYALS-KING-HARALD-FUNERAL.jpg">© Claudia Greco, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Trump declines to back Saudi Arabia as US officials reportedly meet Iran-backed Houthis in Oman</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/trump-declines-to-back-saudi-arabia-as-us-officials-reportedly-meet-iran-backed-houthis-in-oman</link><description>
US officials met representatives of Yemen's Houthis in Oman over the weekend, five sources familiar with the matter said, days after the Iran-backed militia seized a strategic ​stretch of the ‌Red Sea coast in a sweeping offensive that routed Saudi-backed forces. U.S. ​President Donald Trump has so far rebuffed pleas from the Saudis for military support fighting the Houthis. FRANCE 24's Fraser Jackson reports from Washington.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e67af742-ae18-11f1-ae71-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7VR3NQ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e67af742-ae18-11f1-ae71-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7VR3NQ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6925b04e-b2c7-11f1-94b8-0bacc0414a65</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 18:47:26 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Stalemate' in Lebanon: Hezbollah justifies weapons, citing Israeli occupation and ongoing attacks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/stalemate-in-lebanon-hezbollah-justifies-weapons-citing-israeli-occupation-and-ongoing-attacks</link><description>
Angela Diffley is pleased to welcome Dr Filippo Dionigi, Senior Lecturer in Politics and International Relations at the University of Bristol. According to Dr. Dionigi, the central obstacle to Hezbollah’s disarmament is not simply the military capacity of the Lebanese state, but the absence of a political settlement capable of making disarmament both legitimate and sustainable. While additional funding and weapons would strengthen the Lebanese Armed Forces, they will not resolve the fundamental political dilemma. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7dac3526-b2b6-11f1-a1e4-1d1125ed9143/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-151052-152026-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7dac3526-b2b6-11f1-a1e4-1d1125ed9143/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-151052-152026-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">83b316ce-b2b6-11f1-8566-3167f41fb792</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 18:44:27 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Perspective</category><title>'Sanctions won’t prevent us from doing our job' says ICC Prosecutor Mame Mandiaye Niang</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20260917-sanctions-won-t-prevent-us-from-doing-our-job-says-icc-prosecutor-mame-mandiaye-niang</link><description>
In this edition of Perspective, the acting Prosecutor of the International Criminal Court tells FRANCE 24 that the court is needed now more than ever to ensure there is no gap for impunity. Mame Mandiaye Niang says the court’s job is to step in if domestic justice systems fail. The Senegalese judge is at the centre of a storm amid sanctions put on the court by the US after its issuing of arrest warrants for Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and former Defence Minister Yoav Gallant over Israel’s actions in Gaza. He explained how the sanctions affect his daily life but says it won’t stop the court doing its job.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/332e1d38-b27b-11f1-8dd7-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/ANGL260917-0940-Live-CS0940.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/332e1d38-b27b-11f1-8dd7-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/ANGL260917-0940-Live-CS0940.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">42111864-b27b-11f1-8a60-a3ca3ffd93d4</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 16:02:51 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Stuart NORVAL</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Gaza documentary 'NAZA' sparks political storm, threats against directors in Israel</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260917-gaza-documentary-naza-sparks-political-storm-in-israel</link><description>
The award-winning documentary "NAZA" featuring anonymous military sources speaking about Israel's mass killing of civilians in Gaza has sparked a political firestorm in Israel. The film's directors and their families have received a wave of threats, while Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu announced a plan for a bill aimed at revoking the citizenship of people who "defame IDF soldiers".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c69183f2-b2b8-11f1-a9f1-61f6f55d211c/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26258555934130.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c69183f2-b2b8-11f1-a9f1-61f6f55d211c/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26258555934130.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e73ee87c-b2ab-11f1-bad0-7d4ece9fee5a</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 15:24:40 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c69183f2-b2b8-11f1-a9f1-61f6f55d211c/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26258555934130.jpg">© Ariel Schalit, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Amnesty accuses Iran of crimes against humanity</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/amnesty-accuses-iran-of-crimes-against-humanity</link><description>
Amnesty International has accused Iranian authorities of committing crimes against humanity during the 2022 Woman, Life, Freedom crackdown, saying more than 500 people, including 71 children, were killed and that the violence disproportionately targeted Kurdish and Baluchi communities. The rights group is urging the UN General Assembly to create an international justice mechanism, arguing that many of the officials it identified remain in positions of power.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b819a372-b2a4-11f1-b669-6db10b20ba37/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-152151-152343-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b819a372-b2a4-11f1-b669-6db10b20ba37/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-152151-152343-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bd4d2396-b2a4-11f1-bcb2-6961acb57df3</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 14:55:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Houthis claim Saudi F-15 kill as Yemen fighting escalates</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/houthis-claim-saudi-f-15-kill-as-yemen-fighting-escalates</link><description>
Yemen's Houthi rebels have released footage they say shows the wreckage of a Saudi F-15 fighter jet, which, if confirmed, would mark the first fighter jet they have shot down. The claim comes as fighting escalates in Yemen, with the Houthis expanding their control around the strategic Bab al-Mandab Strait and the UN urging both sides to return to negotiations.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4e0dde78-b2a2-11f1-98e8-991cccd3bb73/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-141009-141202-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4e0dde78-b2a2-11f1-98e8-991cccd3bb73/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-141009-141202-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1db0b8ba-b2a5-11f1-853c-6148f6ccb5da</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 14:53:00 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Lebanon on Paris talks : 'the general sentiment here is very little hope'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/lebanon-on-paris-talks-the-general-sentiment-here-is-very-little-hope</link><description>
Lebanese President Joseph Aoun is in Paris for talks with Emmanuel Macron, but on the ground many Lebanese say they have little hope after months of war with Israel, the continued occupation of parts of southern Lebanon and uncertainty over regional tensions. FRANCE 24's Renée David reports from Beirut on hopes that Aoun and Macron can rally international backing and secure a framework agreement to help stabilise the country.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d9744b0-b2a4-11f1-815e-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-141204-141501-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d9744b0-b2a4-11f1-815e-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-141204-141501-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">93091b44-b2a4-11f1-a558-7f456347e22f</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 14:46:07 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Lebanon: UNIFIL withdrawal at the heart of Paris talks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/lebanon-unifil-withdrawal-at-the-heart-of-paris-talks</link><description>
Emmanuel Macron welcomes Lebanese President Joseph Aoun and Jordan's King Abdullah II to Paris today for talks on Lebanon's security and international support for the Lebanese army. The meeting comes as France pushes to prevent a security vacuum ahead of UNIFIL's planned withdrawal at the end of 2026, with Israeli strikes continuing in southern Lebanon and concerns growing over who will secure the border. FRANCE 24's Luke Shrago has the latest.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d493f712-b297-11f1-8ba9-07ed91e97eb2/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-130744-131215-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d493f712-b297-11f1-8ba9-07ed91e97eb2/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-130744-131215-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d9f5b718-b297-11f1-92f4-d3e82812b02d</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 13:23:41 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Syrian court issues first sentences over 2025 massacres of Alawites</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260917-syrian-court-issues-first-sentences-over-2025-massacres-of-alawites</link><description>
Syria's judiciary on Thursday issued its first verdicts over the massacres of Alawites on the Syrian coast last year, sentencing a former member of government forces to 20 years in prison. A supporter of deposed president Bashar al-Assad received a death sentence and another was sentenced to life in jail. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/66fe5ee0-414b-11f0-b396-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000_36ZR2LG.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/66fe5ee0-414b-11f0-b396-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000_36ZR2LG.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">48306f1c-b274-11f1-b38e-275430d05d0c</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 09:13:50 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/66fe5ee0-414b-11f0-b396-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000_36ZR2LG.jpg">© Delil Souleiman, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Lebanon: Emmanuel Macron welcomes Joseph Aoun to Paris for Middle East talks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/lebanon-emmanuel-macron-welcomes-joseph-aoun-to-paris-for-middle-east-talks</link><description>
French President Emmanuel Macron is hosting Lebanese President Joseph Aoun in Paris for talks focused on Lebanon's security and wider Middle East tensions, with Jordan's King Abdullah II also taking part in the meeting. FRANCE 24's Luke Shrago and Kethevane Gorjestani have the analysis from Paris.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c694a296-b270-11f1-b93b-991cccd3bb73/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-100132-101156-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c694a296-b270-11f1-b93b-991cccd3bb73/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-100132-101156-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cb7932a4-b270-11f1-b8db-a5077b1dbff6</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 08:48:01 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Lebanon: Macron, Aoun and King Abdullah II hold security talks in Paris</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/lebanon-macron-aoun-and-king-abdullah-ii-hold-security-talks-in-paris</link><description>
Emmanuel Macron is hosting Lebanese President Joseph Aoun and Jordan's King Abdullah II in Paris for talks on Lebanon's security and international support for the Lebanese army. The meeting comes as concerns grow over Israel's continued strikes in southern Lebanon and the possible end of the UNIFIL peacekeeping mission, with France seeking a "clear, credible and realistic" plan to back Lebanon through funding, equipment and military training.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/422cc902-b26b-11f1-83de-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-090233-090415-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/422cc902-b26b-11f1-83de-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-090233-090415-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4ad76774-b26b-11f1-89f3-e9e6715e3397</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 07:59:59 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Middle East : Trump plans $2.8bn arms package for Israel amid Gaza war</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east-trump-plans-2-8bn-arms-package-for-israel-amid-gaza-war</link><description>
The Trump administration is reportedly preparing a $2.8 billion arms package for Israel, including 40,000 bombs, as Israel continues strikes in Gaza despite last October's ceasefire. The proposed deal would further strengthen Israel's military capabilities and revive deliveries of 2,000-pound bombs that had previously been paused over concerns about civilian casualties.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/634b4612-b26c-11f1-b404-3df65e1cd14d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-090447-090628-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/634b4612-b26c-11f1-b404-3df65e1cd14d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-090447-090628-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">68e45492-b26c-11f1-b49c-391e5dc51093</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 07:55:54 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>US allows Iranian delegation to attend UN General Assembly</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260917-middle-east-live-paris-talks-lebanese-army-unifil-israel-iran-yemen</link><description>
The US State Department said Thursday it had approved visas for top Iranian officials, including President Masoud Pezeshkian and Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi, to attend next week’s UN General Assembly in New York. The delegation will be smaller than last year and will face some travel restrictions. Read our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.
