Ed Sheeran's tour of North and South America has been roiled by the decision this week to drop Macklemore as an opener because of the rapper's onstage pro-Palestinian comments. Since then, all of Sheeran's other supporting acts have dropped out, including a group that backs Sheeran up during part of the show. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis speaks with David Jackson, Professor of Political Science at Bowling Green State University about the issue.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/289eec80-b212-11f1-9582-991cccd3bb73/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-223104-224345-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/289eec80-b212-11f1-9582-991cccd3bb73/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-223104-224345-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2e4064b6-b212-11f1-a6ef-b54447e21b73</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 21:31:54 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Amnesty says Iran committed 'crimes against humanity' in protests crackdown</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/amnesty-says-iran-committed-crimes-against-humanity-in-protests-crackdown</link><description>
Iranian authorities committed crimes against humanity in the crackdown on 2022 protests that left hundreds dead, Amnesty International said Wednesday, adding Tehran's suppression of new demonstrations this year bore the "same hallmarks" but on an even wider scale. FRANCE 24's Mark Owen speaks with Amnesty International Iran Researcher Raha Bahreini. She calls for the establishment of an international criminal justice mechanism to prosecute those responsible for the crimes.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d0fc1bd2-b208-11f1-b188-0dbbad64a63b/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-213118-213957-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d0fc1bd2-b208-11f1-b188-0dbbad64a63b/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-213118-213957-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d6ac8bde-b208-11f1-a8b6-b590cfce5101</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 20:09:08 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Saudi Arabia accuses Houthis of targeting Mecca, calls it a 'red line'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260916-saudi-arabia-accuses-houthis-of-targeting-mecca-calling-it-a-red-line</link><description>
Saudi Arabia accused Yemen’s Houthis on Wednesday of launching an attack on the holy city of Mecca, which the Iran-backed rebels denied. Saudi Arabia, a US ally which has been the target of large-scale Houthi strikes since early September, declared Mecca a “red line” as it slid deeper into the new front of the Iran war.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/824ac65c-b206-11f1-83d2-757719c1152f/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C8H2794.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/824ac65c-b206-11f1-83d2-757719c1152f/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C8H2794.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2d6ae492-b200-11f1-a3a7-0f4fc758a6c4</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 20:08:24 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/824ac65c-b206-11f1-83d2-757719c1152f/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C8H2794.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Saudi Arabia accuses Houthis of targeting Mecca, warns of 'red line'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/saudi-arabia-accuses-houthis-of-targeting-mecca-warns-of-red-line</link><description>
Saudi Arabia accused Yemen's Houthis on Wednesday of launching a "cowardly" attack targeting Islam's holy city of Mecca, sparking outrage across the Muslim world. The Houthis swiftly rejected as a "lie" Riyadh's statement that it had shot down a drone heading towards Mecca, which attracts millions of pilgrims each year. FRANCE 24's Emerald Maxwell reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7b49831a-5730-11f1-b727-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26142709290637.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7b49831a-5730-11f1-b727-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26142709290637.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0572697c-b202-11f1-8718-db5ba3fdb880</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 19:13:38 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Washington set to approve $2.8 bn arms package for Israel</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/washington-set-to-approve-2-8-bn-arms-package-for-israel</link><description>
The US federal government is on track to approve a $2.8 billion arms package for Israel, US media reported Tuesday, with the sale of 40,000 one-ton bombs among the largest munitions packages sold in recent years. The Washington Post said the package -- funded with US taxpayer dollars -- featured some of the most destructive munitions in Western arsenals, including 20,000 MK-84s, 20,000 BLU-117s, and 20,000 I-2000 Penetrator warheads. FRANCE 24's Selina Sykes reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/942153e2-b1fb-11f1-bd55-3df65e1cd14d/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-17306261656aaade6612d4f8-79538850.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/942153e2-b1fb-11f1-bd55-3df65e1cd14d/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-17306261656aaade6612d4f8-79538850.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2e26b3bc-b1fa-11f1-bd40-b312af735817</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 18:24:15 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Perspective</category><title>Emergency doctor on the challenges of caring for civilians in conflict zones</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20260916-emergency-doctor-on-the-challenges-of-caring-for-civilians-in-conflict-zones</link><description>
For humanitarian doctors and healthcare workers operating in active conflict zones, the challenges are seemingly endless: from so-called "double tap" strikes that put emergency workers at risk, to roadblocks, evacuation orders and even the positioning of humanitarian organisations in the political debate. Pierre Catoire, emergency doctor and vice-president of Mehad – A French NGO dedicated to healthcare in conflict zones – speaks to FRANCE 24 about how medical professionals go about their work in such conditions.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6c3a232e-b1bd-11f1-9872-e59e88953996/w:1024/p:16x9/ANGL260916-1015-Live-CS1015.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6c3a232e-b1bd-11f1-9872-e59e88953996/w:1024/p:16x9/ANGL260916-1015-Live-CS1015.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f89b6cc4-b1bd-11f1-a31e-11ba3a3e976d</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 14:55:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Carys GARLAND</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Amnesty says Iran committed 'crimes against humanity' in 2022 protests crackdown</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260916-amnesty-international-says-iran-committed-crimes-against-humanity-in-2022-protests-crackdown</link><description>
In a report released Wednesday, Amnesty International said Iranian authorities committed “crimes against humanity” during the violent crackdown on the 2022 protests known as the movement “Woman, Life, Freedom” that was sparked by the death of Mahsa Amini.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fa676064-b1b1-11f1-9e38-53b7617a3a51/w:1024/p:16x9/000-32M77DV.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fa676064-b1b1-11f1-9e38-53b7617a3a51/w:1024/p:16x9/000-32M77DV.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">34c09a24-b1b1-11f1-84e5-cd7763d25794</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 09:30:07 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fa676064-b1b1-11f1-9e38-53b7617a3a51/w:1024/p:16x9/000-32M77DV.jpg">© AFP, X</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Houthis report Saudi strikes as Riyadh accuses them of targeting Mecca</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260916-middle-east-live-saudi-arabia-accuses-houthi-rebels-of-launching-a-drone-strike-on-mecca</link><description>
Yemen's Houthis reported fresh Saudi airstrikes on Wednesday, as Riyadh accused the group of launching a "cowardly" attack targeting Islam's holy city of Mecca. The Houthis swiftly rejected as a "lie" Riyadh's early morning statement that it had shot down a drone heading towards Mecca, but the accusation prompted a chorus of outrage from around the Muslim world. Read our blog to see how the day's events unfolded.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e76953e8-b218-11f1-8a7d-0dbbad64a63b/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-16T134945Z-1339566980-RC2DKNANTNM5-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-YEMEN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e76953e8-b218-11f1-8a7d-0dbbad64a63b/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-16T134945Z-1339566980-RC2DKNANTNM5-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-YEMEN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">589f5008-b174-11f1-bf7c-cffccd86975a</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 02:14:27 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e76953e8-b218-11f1-8a7d-0dbbad64a63b/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-16T134945Z-1339566980-RC2DKNANTNM5-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-YEMEN.jpg">© Houthi Military Media, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Saudi crown prince seeks neighbours' backing as Houthi attacks rattle Red Sea oil routes</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/saudi-crown-prince-seeks-neighbours-backing-as-houthi-attacks-rattle-red-sea-oil-routes</link><description>
Saudi Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman and Egyptian President Abdel Fattah al-Sisi called for free and secure navigation in the Red Sea during talks in Cairo on Tuesday, as the kingdom vowed to respond "firmly" to attacks by Yemen's Houthis. The two regional powers discussed the threat posed by the Iran-backed group's control over the Bab al-Mandab Strait. FRANCE 24's Emerald Maxwell has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2dc7031c-b133-11f1-85df-3ff9dda05487/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260915-201351-201546-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2dc7031c-b133-11f1-85df-3ff9dda05487/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260915-201351-201546-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">75f584ec-b133-11f1-a540-072a85fb6bfd</guid><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 18:37:00 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
